  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Tailwind Configuration**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/index.css` to grasp Tailwind 4\'s configuration. My focus is pinpointing custom fonts, variables, and utilities referenced in the HTML to replicate the UI\'s look, as seen in the provided screenshot designs. I\'m cross-referencing to ensure complete accuracy.\n\n\n**Identifying Key Customizations**\n\nI\'ve got the HTML data. It outlines the font stack: Montserrat for display, Inter for body and labels. Dark/Light mode is handled via the `.dark` class, with specific color values defined for primary, secondary, tertiary, and background. Additionally, the project uses glassmorphism, scrims for readability, and neon glow effects. Now I need to check how Tailwind handles these in v4.\n\n\n**Implementing Tailwind Variables & Classes**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the Tailwind setup. I\'m importing the Google Fonts for Montserrat and Inter directly into `src/index.css`. Alongside this, I\'m defining custom utility classes for glass panels, scrim gradients, scrollbar modifications, neon glow effects, and both light and dark mode color schemes to match the provided specifications. The plan is to create these variables using `@theme` and CSS variables.\n\nI\'m also setting up the application structure. I\'m adding `src/types.ts` for defining data structures. Then, I am adding `/src/data/mockData.ts` to be a rich data library to store all the movie information and reference images. Finally I\'m adding a context `src/context/AppContext.tsx`.\n\n\n**Defining App Component Structure**\n\nI am now outlining the application\'s core data and component architecture. I am organizing the information into various key areas such as movie data, user profile, and app state, including details on dark mode and movie playback. My current focus is on building components like `Header.tsx` for the navigation bar, with glassmorphic styling, and the `BottomNav.tsx` component to handle responsive navigation.\n\n\n**Structuring UI Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on UI components, starting with `/src/components/HeroBanner.tsx`, a high-impact section with scrims and CTAs. Next, I\'m working on `/src/components/MovieCard.tsx`, reusable cards featuring ratings, badges, progress bars, and hover effects. Finally, I\'ll structure `/src/components/MovieDetails.tsx`, designing a full-screen view incorporating all the necessary elements, as well as `/src/components/SearchScreen.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Feature Screens**\n\nI am now focusing on new feature screen designs. I\'m building a horizontal scroller for \"Popular Searches,\" and a \"Browse Categories\" bento grid. I\'m also planning a live search screen with filter capabilities. In addition, I will be working on a profile view to match the provided screenshots. The profile will have a header and stat grid with details of watch time, and continue-watching features. I am also working on interactive subscription cards. Finally, the design of a full-fidelity video player modal is underway.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 708613587
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
